 "turnNotes": {
  "1": "D-Day, 9 September: the Fifth Army lands in the Gulf of Salerno. Roll the Invasion table for each beach.",
  "5": "Historically: the 82nd Airborne drops into the beachhead overnight (13-14 Sept).",
  "6": "Historically: the main German counterattack on the beachhead (14 Sept).",
  "8": "Historically: the battleships Valiant and Warspite arrive; the Germans begin to draw off (16 Sept).",
  "11": "The Eighth Army arrives from Calabria at the south edge.",
  "12": "Historically: the Fifth and Eighth Armies join near Auletta; Potenza falls (20 Sept). The 36th Division goes into army reserve.",
  "19": "Historically: Foggia falls to the Eighth Army (27 Sept).",
  "23": "Historically: Naples falls on 1 October.",
  "24": "Historically: the commandos land at Termoli (3 October); the 16th Panzer Division counter-attacks there until the 6th. Also: Corsica is liberated by the Free French.",
  "27": "The Race for Naples and Foggia ends.",
  "28": "Historically: Italy declares war on Germany.",
  "29": "Historically: the Canadians take Campobasso (14 October).",
  "35": "The Winter Line begins. Historically: the Eighth Army attacks across the Trigno and takes San Salvo (3 November).",
  "36": "Naples: +1 Allied supply.",
  "43": "Historically: the Eighth Army's main attack across the Sangro (27-28 November).",
  "45": "Historically: the Luftwaffe strikes Bari harbor, 17 ships sunk.",
  "46": "Historically: the Canadians cross the Moro (6-9 December). Naples: +2 Allied supply.",
  "51": "Historically: the battle for Ortona begins (21 December); the town is cleared on the 28th.",
  "54": "The campaign ends."
 },
